  "details": "Let's say this is the input field with the caret (the flashing line):\n\n|\n\nAnd I want to type \"Hello.\" Normally, after typing \"H\", the field should look like:\n\nH|\n\nHowever, it will sometimes look like:\n\n|H\n\nCausing the rest of the letters to be out of place and the word misspelled as \"elloH\". I'm not sure if the caret position not updating is caused by lag, or maybe because I have the chatbox mapped to the mic key, but this is a very annoying bug especially when the keyboard is already so unresponsive (please also look into why sometimes keys can't be pressed unless you nudge the keyboard down a little. Is it interfering with the personal mirror?)",
